From 70edc2fdd59825a8e857de1d0a050d5082f831d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:00:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 083/109] ASoC: codecs: sc2723: headphones and microphone

Add the headphone output and the main microphone capture path:

- Headphones: DACL/DACR to HPL/HPR through their mixers, the class-G
  supply (charge pump LDO, G1 63/G2 7 as the vendor HAL) and the
  headphone PA with its 130 ms enable delay and switch-over to the
  class-G stage, as the vendor driver does for a chip that is not
  version E.
- Microphone: MIC bias, boost, ADC mixers, ADC PGAs, the AD clock and
  input buffer, and the digital ADC enables, with a "Capture" stream on
  the DAI (8, 16, 32 and 48 kHz).
- Controls with dB scales from the vendor driver: headphone volume,
  mic boost and ADC capture volume. The ADC step of 0.75 dB is confirmed
  by measurement; the mic boost steps measured about 4 dB instead of the
  nominal 6 dB.

Tested on the gtelwifi: capture runs at 48 kHz mono and stereo,
also together with playback; a quiet speaker tone shows up in the
recording 35 dB over the noise floor and disappears with the mic bias
off. The headphone path powers up with the class-G values of the
vendor HAL (no headphones connected yet).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
